  "rules": {
    "infinity": "Strict JSON has no infinities: an infinite value is written as null, in JSON and in Arrow alike, only in the columns whose manifest entry has null_means '-inf' (payouts.lower: the zero row of a below_attachment 'zero' run, param_index -1, covers the index range below the attachment). Any other infinite value is refused at export.",
    "nan": "NaN is never written. In a column whose store schema allows undefined values it is written as null, and the column's manifest entry gives its null count and what null means there; in any other column it is refused at export. A column has at most one meaning of null.",
    "types": "Integers are 32-bit (Arrow JS reads 64-bit integers as BigInt); strings are dictionary-encoded UTF-8 with the narrowest signed index (int8, int16 or int32); floats are 64-bit.",
    "arrow": "Tables are Arrow IPC files (.arrow), uncompressed, one record batch: Quarto OJS reads them with FileAttachment(path).arrow().",
    "budget": "Every file, the manifest included, fits max_file_bytes, and the data files together fit max_bundle_bytes (both in bytes). Over budget is an error at export, never a truncation.",
    "checksums": "Every data file is listed under files with its size in bytes and the SHA-256 of its bytes; the manifest itself is not."
  }
